    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48845" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θητ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be a serf</i> or <i>labourer</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λαομέδοντι . . θητεύσαμεν εἰς ἐνιαυτόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.444
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.357
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θητευέμεν ἄλλῳ, ἀνδρὶ παρ᾽ ἀκλήρῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.489
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				77
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Euthphr.</u>
				4c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				359d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Piet.</u>
				63
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ἐπὶ μισθῷ παρά τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.137
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. εἰς τὸ τεῖχος</span>
			<i>labour</i> at it, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>Her.</u>
				12a
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. Παλλάδι καὶ Παφίῃ</span>”
				<i>serve,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					5.292.12
				</span></i>
			 (Paul. Sil.).</div>
